The symbolic icons under scalable/actions/ are taken verbatim from the GNOME
Project's adwaita-icon-theme:

    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/adwaita-icon-theme

They are dual licensed under the GNU LGPL v3 or the Creative Commons
Attribution-Share Alike 3.0 United States License, at your option. Upstream
states that attributing the artwork to the "GNOME Project" is sufficient.

    CC-BY-SA 3.0: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
    LGPL v3:      https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html

Artwork copyright the GNOME Project. The rest of Sleek remains under the
repository's own licence; these files keep the licence above.

They are vendored because the Android build packages only GTK's own small
built-in icon set — adwaita-icon-theme is not one of pixiewood's dependency
wraps, so every icon name outside GTK's set renders as a broken image on
device. See meson.build, which installs this tree into share/icons.

Vendored icons:
    application-exit-symbolic.svg     (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    call-start-symbolic.svg           (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    call-stop-symbolic.svg            (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    document-edit-symbolic.svg        (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    mail-reply-sender-symbolic.svg    (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    sidebar-show-symbolic.svg         (Adwaita/symbolic/actions)
    system-users-symbolic.svg         (Adwaita/symbolic/legacy)
